# Testing

- Use RED → GREEN → REFACTOR for behavior changes.
- Unit tests cover domain decisions and edge cases; integration tests cover API contracts and adapters; E2E tests cover user-visible outcomes.
- Minimum coverage is 80% for branches, functions, lines, and statements. Never narrow include globs just to inflate coverage.
- Tests are isolated and deterministic; use unique identifiers and semantic locators.
- Every bug fix starts with a reproducer.
- Critical desktop and iPad/WebKit flows must pass before handoff.
- Database changes require pgTAP tests for tables, policies, triggers, and invariants.
